#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook for the drovr plugin — the per-turn gate.
#
# Injects a small card (<=600 bytes) before every user turn, re-asserting the
# routing rule the SessionStart reflex established: even a 1% chance a drovr:*
# skill applies means invoking it. A SessionStart injection is one prompt at the
# top of a session and scrolls out from under the agent as the context fills;
# the gate is what keeps the discipline reachable at turn 200.
#
# This hook is deliberately thin: it resolves the plugin root and delegates every
# decision to `drovr reflex --gate`, which reads the `[reflex]` config (`enabled`,
# `per_turn`) and the transcript named on stdin, and prints the hook JSON or
# nothing at all. Keeping the logic in the CLI keeps it unit-testable.
#
# TWO DELIBERATE DIFFERENCES FROM hooks/session-start. Both are load-bearing;
# neither is an oversight to be tidied away.
#
#   1. NO DROVR_PHASE SUPPRESSION. The SessionStart reflex no-ops inside a
#      drovr-spawned phase because the phase agent runs on its injected briefing.
#      The gate does the opposite: a phase is exactly where the discipline has to
#      hold, and a phase agent's briefing scrolls out of the window like anything
#      else. Adding an `if [ -n "${DROVR_PHASE:-}" ]` block here would silence
#      the gate precisely where it matters most — and the CLI does not check
#      DROVR_PHASE at all, so this script is the only place that asymmetry can be
#      got wrong.
#
#   2. STDIN IS PASSED THROUGH. Claude Code writes the hook payload — including
#      `transcript_path` — to stdin, and that path is the gate's only evidence
#      that the previous turn already invoked a drovr:* skill and needs no card.
#      `exec` hands this process's stdin to drovr unchanged. Nothing in this
#      script may consume stdin (no `read`, no heredoc): a script that ate the
#      payload would leave the gate emitting on every single turn, which looks
#      exactly like a healthy hook.

set -euo pipefail

# NO PLUGIN-ROOT RESOLUTION, deliberately. hooks/session-start resolves
# CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT because it must locate skills/using-drovr/SKILL.md on disk.
# The gate card is a `const` compiled into the CLI, which reads
# CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT nowhere at all — so the same block here would be dead code
# that still fails: `PLUGIN_ROOT="$(cd "${SCRIPT_DIR}/.." && pwd)"` under
# `set -e` aborts the hook if that directory is unreadable or the script is
# reached through a broken symlink, silencing the gate for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the gate. That is fail-CLOSED inside a fail-open design.
# If a future card ever reads from disk, resolve the root then.
# Pinned by `user_prompt_hook_needs_no_plugin_root`.

# Delegate to the drovr CLI. $DROVR_BIN overrides the binary — tests point it at
# the freshly built binary; in a real session `drovr` is on PATH. `exec` hands
# drovr's stdin, stdout and exit status to Claude Code directly, so a missing
# binary fails loudly (non-zero) rather than injecting nothing, which is
# indistinguishable from a legitimately suppressed turn.
exec "${DROVR_BIN:-drovr}" reflex --gate
